==Arabic==

===Etymology 1===
{{ety|ar|id=to maul}}
From {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*paras-}}, compare {{cog|gez|ፈረሰ|t=to demolish}}, {{cog|he|פָּרַס|t=to divide|tr=pārás}}, {{cog|arc|פְּרַס|t=to divide|tr=pᵊras}}, {{cog|akk|parāsum|𒋻|tr=parāsum|t=to cut off}}. From the root {{ar-root|ف ر س}}.

Also, from {{inh|ar|sem-pro|*paraš-}}, {{cog|arc|פְרַשׁ|tr=pᵊraš|t=to cut off}}.

Further, {{cog|ar|فَرَصَ|t=to slit}}, {{cog|he|פָּרַץ|tr=pāraṣ|t=to breach}}, {{cog|akk|parāṣum|𒉺𒊏𒍮|tr=parāṣum|t=to lie, to break an oath or breach trust}}, {{cog|gez|ፈረጸ|t=to break open}}, {{cog|uga|𐎔𐎗𐎕|t=to open}}, as well as {{cog|ar|فَرَضَ|t=to notch}}.

Also, {{cog|ar|فَرَقَ|t=to separate}}, widespread in Semitic.

Also, {{cog|ar|فَرَثَ|t=to scatter}}, {{cog|arc|פְּרַת|tr=pᵊraṯ|t=to tear apart}}

